preConditionHook:
// An early bar of the session closes beyond the high (long) or low (short) of
// the session's FIRST bar. offsetBars = 1 is the second bar of the day
// breaking the first bar's high; offsetBars = 2 is the third bar doing it.
//
// The gate is what makes it a once-a-day test rather than an every-bar one:
// the bar offsetBars back must itself be the session's first bar, i.e. its
// wall-clock close date differs from the bar before it -- the same date
// slicing CloseWithinAtrOfVwap uses, read at an offset
// (EL Date[offsetBars] > Date[offsetBars + 1], ordinary series history of the
// Date data word). So the rule can only fire on the bar exactly
// offsetBars + 1 into the session.
//
// Not CloseAbovePriorHigh, which is the price half at every bar of the chart.
// Intraday bars only -- on a daily series every bar starts its own session
// and the rule degenerates to CloseAbovePriorHigh at that lookback.//
// windowBars WIDENS THE GATE INTO A WINDOW (added in the final review, in place
// of a separate SessionFirstBarBreakout rule): the scan accepts the session's
// first bar at any offset from offsetBars to offsetBars + windowBars - 1, so
// the current bar may be any of the first windowBars bars after it and still
// break that first bar's extreme. At windowBars = 1 only offsetBars is scanned
// and the rule is exactly what it was. At most one offset in the window can be
// a session start, so the loop finds at most one level.
// Deepest bar touched: offsetBars + windowBars.
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration
// is a redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
// Every one is fully assigned each bar before it is read.
sessOffset = (int)offsetBars;
sessStart = false;
brkUp = false;
brkDn = false;
for (int k = sessOffset; k <= sessOffset + (int)windowBars - 1; ++k) {
    if (day_of(ctx.Time(k)) > day_of(ctx.Time(k + 1))) {
        sessStart = true;
        if (el_gt(close[0], high[k])) brkUp = true;
        if (el_lt(close[0], low[k])) brkDn = true;
    }
}
